# ergo test cannot build a Model for the member law of Pipeline: a Model
# holds an actor that a context opens (Open needs a Runner and a
# Scheduler). pipeline/laws.ergo's ModelTakesEachCommandOnce opens one and
# runs the same body against it.
skip law Pipeline.DuplicateIsNoop for Model: its values have no generator: actor.Actor[domain.Ledger[Desk, Entry], Signal, Decision[domain.Ledger[Desk, Entry], domain.Receipt], NoSuchRun | run.BadLength | run.Closed | run.WrongStage | run.WrongState] is an operation type with no builder: neither actor nor actortest, as this package sees them, declares a New<X> with no row whose X provides it; bind one in a named context of a test file, let Name = context { Pipeline: … }, and the law runs under it
# ergo test cannot build the generated Client (an rpc.Conn comes only from
# rpc.Dial or rpc.Loopback). surfaces/laws.ergo's TransportsTakeEachCommandOnce
# serves a Model in process and runs the same body against its Client.
skip law pipeline.Pipeline.DuplicateIsNoop for Client: its values have no generator: rpc.Conn has an unexported field, so only package rpc builds it; use rpc.Dial or rpc.Loopback; bind one in a named context of a test file, let Name = context { pipeline.Pipeline: … }, and the law runs under it
# ergo test cannot build the hub's Client (its send is a function value,
# which has no generator). The hub's law ClientIsCall holds that a Client
# whose send is Call answers as the bound provider does, and each
# transport's law Agrees holds its Wire to Call (AF0, AF1).
skip law pipeline.Pipeline.DuplicateIsNoop for Client: its values have no generator: func(Request) Outcome is a function type; bind one in a named context of a test file, let Name = context { pipeline.Pipeline: … }, and the law runs under it
